# The first slice runs entirely locally in the browser (IndexedDB); no variables
# are required. Cloud (optional browser Supabase) is enabled only when all three
# public values below are valid for the origin the app is served from:
#
# - the URL must be https on a *.supabase.co host (http/https on localhost also works),
# - the key must be a publishable (`sb_publishable_…`) or legacy anon key — never a
#   service-role key, which must never reach the browser,
# - the served origin must appear exactly in the allowed origins list (also allow each
#   /auth/callback URL in Supabase Auth).
#
# Without valid public config the app stays fully local-only: no auth, no cloud
# requests, and no cloud chrome.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_REPLACE_ME
# VITE_AUTH_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:4173,https://your-deployment.example
